"). # Why this is one nested","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"policy rather than nine fields Every field here is a term of a single decision — ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"do we","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fetch a stranger’s URL and make a client out of what comes back","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — and none of them means","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anything without [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::enabled"},{"text":"]. A tenant that states a CIMD posture states all of it; a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant that states none inherits its organization’s whole posture rather than half of one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is the only merge that cannot produce a combination neither party wrote. # The two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields that can widen, and the seven that cannot [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::enabled"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::allow_http"},{"text":"]","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ordered"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": a tenant may turn either off but never on, exactly as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dynamic_registration"},{"text":" may only move down its ladder. Everything else names ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"domains or ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" bounds, and there is no sense in which one tenant’s list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trusted publishers is stricter than another’s — the same argument [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OidcPolicy"},{"text":"] already","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts"},{"text":". # Every bound here is a security control","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::max_metadata_bytes"},{"text":"], [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::min_cache_secs"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::max_cache_secs"},{"text":"] are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tuning knobs. They are, respectively, the ceiling on a read from an attacker-chosen URL, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"floor under how often that read may be repeated, and the ceiling on how long its result may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be trusted. Each is clamped again in code against the three constants above, so a settings","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row written by hand cannot lift them.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CimdPolicy"}]}}}